  "claim": "The music and lyrics of a fifty word national anthem author is one of the most participants of a country's National Revival. Vingis Park is the largest park in Butuan in this country.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Vincas Kudirka. Sentence: Vincas Kudirka (31 December [O.S. 19 December] 1858 – 16 November [O.S. 4 November] 1899 ) was a Lithuanian poet and physician, and the author of both the music and lyrics of the Lithuanian National Anthem, \"Tautiška giesmė\".\nPage: Tautiška giesmė. Sentence: Tautiška giesmė (\"The National Hymn\"; ] ) is the national anthem of Lithuania, also known by its opening words \"Lietuva, Tėvyne mūsų\" (official translation of the lyrics: \"Lithuania, Our Homeland\", literally: \"Lithuania, Our Fatherland\") and as \"Lietuvos himnas\" (Hymn of Lithuania).\nPage: Tautiška giesmė. Sentence: The fifty-word poem was a condensation of Kudirka's conceptions of the Lithuanian state, the Lithuanian people, and their past.\nPage: Lithuanian National Revival. Sentence: Most active participants of national revival were Vincas Kudirka, Jonas Basanavičius and others.\nPage: Vingis Park. Sentence: Vingis Park is the largest park in Vilnius, Lithuania.",
  "evidence_text": "Page: Vincas Kudirka. Sentence: Vincas Kudirka (31 December [O.S. 19 December] 1858 – 16 November [O.S. 4 November] 1899 ) was a Lithuanian poet and physician, and the author of both the music and lyrics of the Lithuanian National Anthem, \"Tautiška giesmė\".\nPage: Tautiška giesmė. Sentence: Tautiška giesmė (\"The National Hymn\"; ] ) is the national anthem of Lithuania, also known by its opening words \"Lietuva, Tėvyne mūsų\" (official translation of the lyrics: \"Lithuania, Our Homeland\", literally: \"Lithuania, Our Fatherland\") and as \"Lietuvos himnas\" (Hymn of Lithuania).\nPage: Tautiška giesmė. Sentence: The fifty-word poem was a condensation of Kudirka's conceptions of the Lithuanian state, the Lithuanian people, and their past.\nPage: Lithuanian National Revival. Sentence: Most active participants of national revival were Vincas Kudirka, Jonas Basanavičius and others.\nPage: Vingis Park. Sentence: Vingis Park is the largest park in Vilnius, Lithuania.",
