        "original_id": "a470a014-bfe5-52d5-8ee9-02b250e73a9b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Vincas Kudirka, Jonas Basanavičius\n- Products: Tautiška giesmė, Lithuanian National Anthem\n- Events: Lithuanian National Revival\n- Places: Vilnius, Lithuania, Vingis Park\n\nFacts:\n- Vincas Kudirka was born on 31 December 1858 and died on 16 November 1899.\n- Vincas Kudirka was a Lithuanian poet and physician.\n- Vincas Kudirka wrote both the music and lyrics of the Lithuanian National Anthem, \"Tautiška giesmė\".\n- Tautiška giesmė is the national anthem of Lithuania.\n- Tautiška giesmė is also known by its opening words \"Lietuva, Tėvyne mūsų\" and as \"Lietuvos himnas\".\n- The fifty-word poem of Tautiška giesmė condensed Vincas Kudirka's conceptions of the Lithuanian state, the Lithuanian people, and their past.\n- Vincas Kudirka and Jonas Basanavičius were among the most active participants in the Lithuanian National Revival.\n- Vingis Park is the largest park in Vilnius, Lithuania.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "0a1d1dba-f013-52be-b4f0-48556c2afb94",
        "text": "Page: Vincas Kudirka. Sentence: Vincas Kudirka (31 December [O.S. 19 December] 1858 – 16 November [O.S. 4 November] 1899 ) was a Lithuanian poet and physician, and the author of both the music and lyrics of the Lithuanian National Anthem, \"Tautiška giesmė\".\nPage: Tautiška giesmė. Sentence: Tautiška giesmė (\"The National Hymn\"; ] ) is the national anthem of Lithuania, also known by its opening words \"Lietuva, Tėvyne mūsų\" (official translation of the lyrics: \"Lithuania, Our Homeland\", literally: \"Lithuania, Our Fatherland\") and as \"Lietuvos himnas\" (Hymn of Lithuania).\nPage: Tautiška giesmė. Sentence: The fifty-word poem was a condensation of Kudirka's conceptions of the Lithuanian state, the Lithuanian people, and their past.\nPage: Lithuanian National Revival. Sentence: Most active participants of national revival were Vincas Kudirka, Jonas Basanavičius and others.\nPage: Vingis Park. Sentence: Vingis Park is the largest park in Vilnius, Lithuania.",
